{
  "title": "Voice Tool",
  "story": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "e796e26399b8ae1a",
      "text": "Speak to the page on the left: record or drop audio, get a transcript, summarise it, and drag the points to where they belong."
    },
    {
      "type": "audionote",
      "id": "20142b3f94057ad2",
      "text": "SUBJECT\nPROMPT: [[Summarise Spoken Notes]]\nPROMPTS: prompt.geek.fish"
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "ae4074e18fbc5530",
      "text": "Open a page, then choose **Voice Tool** from the \u2630 menu: it opens to the right and takes that page as its subject. **Speak** \u2014 pause and resume as you think \u2014 then **Stop**, and the words are transcribed. Choose a prompt, **Summarise**, and edit the result. The notes get a **page title**, *Open Questions Notes* for a page called Open Questions, which you can change; **a page it is waiting for** lists the page's red links, and choosing one names the notes after it, so saving turns that link blue."
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "fdbec7b91aded615",
      "text": "**Open as ghost page** shows the notes under that title, each point its own item, to drag wherever it belongs. **Save page & link it**, the default (in blue; Enter in the page title presses it), makes the ghost a real page and puts a `[[link]]` to it on the page to the left. **Start over** clears the recording, transcript and summary. The rest \u2014 prompts, the shape of the page a note makes, phones, the directives \u2014 is in the [[Voice Tool Guide]]."
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "677c4fe53bb423cf",
      "text": "# Where Things Go"
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "168ef144ce94cd84",
      "text": "> Nothing reaches the wiki until you save."
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "36cfbd9003db33a6",
      "text": "An unsaved recording, its transcript and its summary live in **this browser** only, and survive following links, closing the tool or reloading, until you save or start over. **Save page & link it** writes one page to **this site** under the title, and one `[[link]]` on the page to the left. The recording itself is **thrown away** after transcription unless you tick *keep the audio*: then it is uploaded to this site's `assets/<folder>` with its transcript `.txt`, and the page gets a player instead of a transcript."
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "841b9b3ac487fde8",
      "text": "# Privacy"
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "e476266ae0ab8bfe",
      "text": "> Your voice goes to one machine to be heard, and the words to one model to be summarised."
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "4b7138f7362a410e",
      "text": "**Who hears the audio.** The farm serving this page \u2014 or, when your browser is on a machine that runs a farm of its own (your laptop with its private farm up), that machine, through the **local door**; the status line says which. On a Mac with MacWhisper open, MacWhisper does the hearing, without filing the recording in its History unless the farm is set to. Either way the audio is transcribed from a temporary folder and deleted, unless you kept it."
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "41a765d67a2fa92e",
      "text": "**Who reads the words.** Summarising sends the transcript, the prompt and the text of the page spoken to, to the model the farm is set up for: Claude (Anthropic's API, or the Claude Code CLI under the farm's own account), a model on the LLM coop's machine, or an Ollama model on your own network where the farm has one. The Model choice beside Summarise names one, or *Auto* lets the farm pick per summary by the question's size: Claude Fable for a question over 48k tokens, the coop's own routing for the rest, Claude when the coop is down \u2014 the same rule the [[Plan Tool]] uses, as far as a summary shares it. The status line says which model wrote the summary and, for Auto, why. The prompt is read from a prompt wiki (prompt.geek.fish unless the item says otherwise)."
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "1f7b0ad2f4cf2ef7",
      "text": "**Who may ask.** A public farm refuses hearing and summarising until its operator allows them. A private farm \u2014 a laptop, a tailnet \u2014 hears for anyone who can reach it, because hearing changes no page; summarising and saving still need the site owner's login."
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "49ed1622b4495e6d",
      "text": "# See"
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "c71e307299ecc1ba",
      "text": "- [[Voice Tool Guide]] \u2014 everything else about the tool\n- [[About Audio Note Plugin]]\n- [[Prompt Format]]"
    }
