    {
      "type": "edit",
      "id": "59810a2e2baeea2a",
      "item": {
        "type": "markdown",
        "id": "59810a2e2baeea2a",
        "text": "The page a note makes starts with the answer: the summary, each point its own item, with no heading or date above it \u2014 the question is the title and the journal keeps the date. It ends with a **# See** section linking back to the page it answers. The recording is **not kept** unless you tick *keep the audio*: it is sent to the farm to be transcribed and deleted there, and the transcript then follows the answer under its own heading. Tick the box, choose the assets folder, and the recording is uploaded \u2014 then an audio player captioned with the title and date, and the folder's assets (the recording and its transcript .txt), take the transcript's place."
      },
      "date": 1790161951325,
      "provenance": "Page shape updated for audionote 0.3.5."
    },
    {
      "type": "edit",
      "id": "59810a2e2baeea2a",
      "item": {
        "type": "markdown",
        "id": "59810a2e2baeea2a",
        "text": "The page a note makes starts with the answer: the summary, each point its own item, with no heading or date above it \u2014 the question is the title and the journal keeps the date. It ends with a **# See** section linking back to the page it answers and to the prompt that shaped the summary; when that prompt was read from the prompt wiki, saving the page forks that site in (a fork event first in the journal, which hands over no credit), so the prompt link leads there. The recording is **not kept** unless you tick *keep the audio*: it is sent to the farm to be transcribed and deleted there, and the transcript then follows the answer under its own heading. Tick the box, choose the assets folder, and the recording is uploaded \u2014 then an audio player captioned with the title and date, and the folder's assets (the recording and its transcript .txt), take the transcript's place."
      },
      "date": 1790162687037,
      "provenance": "Prompt link + fork seeding, audionote 0.3.6."
    },
    {
      "type": "add",
      "id": "2681c65fff5bc20e",
      "item": {
        "type": "markdown",
        "id": "2681c65fff5bc20e",
        "text": "# Public Sites"
      },
      "after": "3f1181bb87fd5292",
      "date": 1791657235776
    },
    {
      "type": "add",
      "id": "1b025103a54df0e9",
      "item": {
        "type": "markdown",
        "id": "1b025103a54df0e9",
        "text": "> A public farm has to say yes first."
      },
      "after": "2681c65fff5bc20e",
      "date": 1791657235776
    },
    {
      "type": "add",
      "id": "2ded458333e4a3cb",
      "item": {
        "type": "markdown",
        "id": "2ded458333e4a3cb",
        "text": "On a farm whose sites are reachable from the open internet, the Voice Tool's three writes \u2014 hear, transcribe and summarise \u2014 are refused with **403 \"is not a private site, and this farm has not been asked to allow writes to public ones\"** until the person running the farm lists them. The Farm plugin asks two questions in order: is this farm willing to take API writes on public sites at all, and may this caller edit this site. The first is answered by the farm's environment, the second by the wiki's own login. A private farm behind a tailnet answers the first with `FARM_API_PRIVATE_SUFFIXES`; a public farm needs `FARM_API_PUBLIC_WRITES=audionote.hear,audionote.transcribe,audionote.summarise`. All three scopes are needed: listing only `audionote.hear` lets the transcript through and fails at summarise. The blanket value `1` would open every page-changing operation on the farm, including table writes and index rebuilds, and should not be used."
      },
      "after": "1b025103a54df0e9",
      "date": 1791657235776
    },
    {
      "type": "add",
      "id": "52c2834762177b95",
      "item": {
        "type": "markdown",
        "id": "52c2834762177b95",
        "text": "Write an **Open Questions** list as red question links, `- [ ] [[Who may open an event?]]`, each question its own item, with no page behind the link. The tool lists them under *a page it is waiting for*, so a spoken answer lands on the page named by the question and turns the link blue."
      },
      "after": "2ded458333e4a3cb",
      "date": 1791657235776
    },
    {
      "type": "edit",
      "id": "fd1919eff8e4fb58",
      "item": {
        "type": "markdown",
        "id": "fd1919eff8e4fb58",
        "text": "An unsaved recording, its transcript and its summary are kept in this browser until you save or start over. Follow a link, edit the page on the left, close the tool or reload \u2014 open the Voice Tool again and they are still there. Nothing is written to the wiki for this. A recording picked up without its transcript \u2014 the farm refused it, or the network dropped \u2014 shows a **\u21bb Transcribe** button, so the audio is sent again rather than spoken again."
      },
      "date": 1791657972286
    },
    {
      "type": "edit",
      "id": "2ded458333e4a3cb",
      "item": {
        "type": "markdown",
        "id": "2ded458333e4a3cb",
        "text": "On a farm whose sites are reachable from the open internet, the Voice Tool's three writes \u2014 hear, transcribe and summarise \u2014 are refused with **403 \"is not a private site, and this farm has not been asked to allow writes to public ones\"** until the person running the farm lists them. The Farm plugin asks two questions in order: is this farm willing to take API writes on public sites at all, and may this caller edit this site. The first is answered by the farm's environment, the second by the wiki's own login. A private farm behind a tailnet answers the first with `FARM_API_PRIVATE_SUFFIXES`; a public farm needs `FARM_API_PUBLIC_WRITES=audionote.hear,audionote.transcribe,audionote.summarise,farm.assetsUpload`. Every scope is needed: listing only `audionote.hear` lets the transcript through and fails at summarise, and *keep the audio* uploads through the Farm plugin's own `farm.assetsUpload`, which is refused until it is listed too. The blanket value `1` would open every page-changing operation on the farm, including table writes and index rebuilds, and should not be used."
      },
      "date": 1791660334142
    },
    {
      "type": "add",
      "id": "40e16ff3d29ba719",
      "item": {
        "type": "markdown",
        "id": "40e16ff3d29ba719",
        "text": "# The Local Door"
      },
      "after": "3f1181bb87fd5292",
      "date": 1791810154561
    },
    {
      "type": "add",
      "id": "a5d9826e45b262df",
      "item": {
        "type": "markdown",
        "id": "a5d9826e45b262df",
        "text": "> The machine you are sitting at hears you first."
      },
      "after": "40e16ff3d29ba719",
      "date": 1791810154561
    },
    {
      "type": "add",
      "id": "684c4c7eafcb5ba4",
      "item": {
        "type": "markdown",
        "id": "684c4c7eafcb5ba4",
        "text": "A recording is normally sent to the farm serving the page. When the browser is on a machine that runs a farm of its own \u2014 a laptop with the private farm up \u2014 the Voice Tool asks that machine first: it probes `http://localhost:4242/system/api.json` once per page load, and if a farm answers whose *hear* operation is gated on the place alone, the recording goes through that **local door** instead. Only the audio travels; the transcript comes back, and the page, the prompt, the summary and any kept audio stay with the farm the page lives on. The status line says where the words were heard \u2014 *transcribing on this Mac, with MacWhisper*, or *on the farm*."
      },
      "after": "a5d9826e45b262df",
      "date": 1791810154561
    },
    {
      "type": "add",
      "id": "a98fea5ed4c38327",
      "item": {
        "type": "markdown",
        "id": "a98fea5ed4c38327",
        "text": "On a Mac the local farm hears with **MacWhisper** whenever that app is open, using the model the app has selected (Parakeet v3, say), and with faster-whisper when it is closed; the choice is made per recording, so opening the app changes the next one. The farm's `AUDIONOTE_ENGINE` can pin either engine; `AUDIONOTE_MACWHISPER_MODEL` names a model in MacWhisper's `engine:id` form, and `AUDIONOTE_MACWHISPER_PERSIST=1` also files each recording in MacWhisper's History."
      },
      "after": "684c4c7eafcb5ba4",
      "date": 1791810154561
    },
    {
      "type": "add",
      "id": "5f6441159815ce82",
      "item": {
        "type": "markdown",
        "id": "5f6441159815ce82",
        "text": "`DOOR: farm` in the item sends every recording to the page's own farm and never probes; `DOOR: http://host:port` names a door of your own. The door answers a page from elsewhere without a login there because *hear* changes no page and keeps nothing \u2014 the farm transcribes from its temporary folder and deletes the file. A public farm still refuses it, as it refuses every write it has not been told to allow."
      },
      "after": "a98fea5ed4c38327",
      "date": 1791810154561
    },
